# -*- mode:org;coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe: configurable per-backend encoding for the CAD subprocess console I/O
#+AUTHOR: Pascal J. Bourguignon
#+DATE: 2026-07-25

Found when the Windows CI vendor:probes:autocad job hit a bootstrap
crash (job 15534319257): the AutoCAD backend read accoreconsole's
stdout/stderr pipe with the default :UTF-8 external-format, but
accoreconsole on a non-UTF-8 (French) Windows writes UTF-16LE, so
`read-char` died with "the octet sequence #(234 0 116) cannot be
decoded" [BOOTSTRAP-FAILED].

* Root cause

alfe has -E (source-file encoding) and -Eterminal (alfe's own terminal
I/O), but NOTHING specifies the encoding of the CAD SUBPROCESS console
I/O. The `uiop:launch-program` call in start-engine (backend-autocad.lisp)
passed no :external-format, and drain-channel (file-protocol.lisp) read
the channel files as hard :utf-8. Neither is knowable ahead of time:
clautolisp/BricsCAD write UTF-8, AutoCAD/accoreconsole writes UTF-16LE
(codepage-dependent).

* Done (fix-alfe-accoreconsole-encoding, alfe 1.6.1)

Defensive, no-config fixes so bootstrap cannot crash:
- drain-channel now reads raw octets and decodes robustly
  (DECODE-CONSOLE-OCTETS: UTF-16LE by BOM/heuristic, UTF-8 BOM, else
  lenient UTF-8 with a per-byte Latin-1 fallback — never signals; ASCII
  verdict lines always survive). Offset is now byte-based. Unit-tested.
- the accoreconsole pipe read uses AUTOCAD-CONSOLE-EXTERNAL-FORMAT
  (default :iso-8859-1, a total decoder; the existing NUL-strip in
  slurp-process-stream cleans UTF-16LE), overridable now via
  $ALFE_AUTOCAD_CONSOLE_ENCODING.

* To design (pjb): per-backend -E CLI options for the subprocess console

pjb wants proper, possibly *different* -E options per backend for the
CAD subprocess console I/O (not just the env-var override shipped
above). Decisions:
- CLI shape: a subprocess-console variant of -E, e.g.
  =--console-encoding ENC= (backend-default), or per backend
  =--autocad-console-encoding= / =--bricscad-console-encoding=?
- default per backend: autocad -> ? (utf-16le vs the robust
  iso-8859-1+auto-detect shipped), bricscad -> utf-8.
- OR pass a codepage option TO accoreconsole so it emits UTF-8
  (investigate accoreconsole flags / a `(setvar)` on the CAD side).
- thread the chosen encoding through start-engine's already-present
  IO-ENCODING param (currently declared ignore in the autocad backend)
  to both the launch-program call and drain-channel.

* Also done (fix-vendor-autocad-runner, alfe 1.6.2)

- accoreconsole DISCOVERY now prefers real AutoCAD over the read-only
  DWG TrueView viewer: both ship accoreconsole.exe and DWG TrueView
  won the descending name sort ("DWG..." > "AutoCAD..."), so on the CI
  runner it launched the viewer — whose config in Program Files is
  read-only/locked, aborting with a MessageBox. %ACCORECONSOLE-PREFERENCE
  ranks AutoCAD before generic before TrueView (unit-tested). If only
  DWG TrueView is installed, install AutoCAD or set
  $AUTOCAD_ACCORECONSOLE to the real binary.
- run-vendor-probes.ps1 copies the drawing to a unique temp name per
  probe (pjb request), so back-to-back / concurrent probes never share
  or lock the same .dwg (or its .dwl/.bak siblings).

* Verify (blocked on the Windows/AutoCAD runner)

Re-run vendor:probes:autocad on master: bootstrap should pass the
decode and reach the probe verdicts. The BricsCAD path likely never hit
this (UTF-8), but apply the same robustness there if a probe surfaces it.
